  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at The Independent in San Francisco on March 8, 2007, sharing the bill with Pony Up! [1]. This recording, taped and transferred by Chris Bellew, captures the full eighteen-song set, which includes tracks like \"Wild Sage,\" \"Broom People,\" and \"California Song\" [1]. It is the only available recording of this specific date and has earned a perfect five-star rating from four listeners [1]. The audio quality is widely praised by reviewers of this specific recording, with one user noting it sounds professional and high-fidelity [2]. Another listener, who stood near the stage, recalled hearing John Vanderslice join the band and mentioned that John Darnielle had never played \"You or Your Memory\" on electric guitar before that night [3]. A third reviewer, who originally recorded the show from the audience, highlighted the presence of Jon Wurster on drums, stating the band had never sounded better [4]. A fourth listener simply described the show and playlist as amazing [5]. The setlist features rare archival appearances, such as \"Peacocks,\" which is the first in the archive and has only four other archived performances [1]. Other rare tracks include \"The House That Dripped Blood,\" \"Half Dead,\" and \"The Boys Are Back In Town\" [1]. This performance is the 109th of 467 Mountain Goats shows in the archive collection [6]. The previous archived show took place the day before at the same venue [6]. Listeners can expect a high-fidelity capture of a significant night for the band, with clear documentation of the recording lineage [1].",
